import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,a5 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Verification plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/workspace-credit-unification/test.md","filePath":"feature/workspace-credit-unification/test.md"}'),r={name:"feature/workspace-credit-unification/test.md"};function n(o,e,l,c,d,p){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="verification-plan" tabindex="-1">Verification plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification plan&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li>Fresh init and ordered migrations give identical tables/columns/indexes/constraints; extension reapplies safely. A conflicting DA-974 schema stops before writes. No public reset/seed API.</li><li>Agency=1000, two Workspace caps=800: overlapping caps allowed; concurrent requests still cannot spend over the Agency or either Workspace budget. NULL caps use Agency funds; zero rejects positive-cost requests; no personal/default-member cap survives. Owner is not exempt from Workspace caps.</li><li>Owner can revise only its Agency&#39;s Workspace cap; expected revision conflict returns conflict; Manager/Creator read only accessible Workspaces. Client cannot generate/change caps. Deactivated/deleted/cross-Agency contexts denied.</li><li>Freeze operation price at reserve. Reuse same key+payload without another dispatch/charge; changed payload conflicts. Price zero/free action behavior remains supported. Different users&#39; request identities do not collide.</li><li>Reserve/settle/release keep wallet, grants, allocations, Workspace counters and append-only journal balanced. Concurrent callbacks settle once. Unknown/timeouts stay held; no refund/re-dispatch merely from deadline expiry.</li><li>Expired Plan available credit is unavailable, Plan used before TOPUP, TOPUP never expires. Late completion debits original Workspace usage period; releasing expired Plan funds does not restore spendable credit. New cycle preserves cap but starts zero usage. Purchased credit remains usable after Subscription expiry.</li><li>Caption generation/history/replay and Video WAITING/poll/failure/callback retain content APIs and avoid legacy double-accounting. No actual paid AI, payment callbacks or public publishing for verification.</li><li>Web displays Workspace caps/used/held/period and Agency wallet consistently; unlimited and zero distinct; errors/stale saves/reload explicit; VI/EN keys parallel, no raw error, keyboard/light/dark/mobile checks.</li><li>Local reset preserves counts of users/agencies/workspaces/campaigns and AI content rows; never touches Mongo. Unlink obsolete financial IDs without deleting AI media/history. No fixed IDs/secrets/local scripts committed.</li></ul><h2 id="results-—-2026-10-22" tabindex="-1">Results — 2026-10-22 <a class="header-anchor" href="#results-—-2026-10-22" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Results — 2026-10-22&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Fresh init succeeds on isolated PostgreSQL 17. Compared columns/defaults/nullability and constraint definitions for 11 unified financial tables against upgraded local: all identical.</li><li>Repeat extension on upgraded local skips without writes. A synthetic legacy user_id reservation schema is rejected before price-table or migration-marker writes.</li><li>29 targeted tests passed, no failures/errors/skips: AiCreditDatabaseTest (8), AiVideoDatabaseTest (6), CreditBalancePostgresTest (3), AgencyBillingPostgresTest (2), AgencyBillingServiceTest (2), BillingSeederTest (3), DataSeederTest (5). These tests compile all test sources and use a disposable loopback DB/mocked AI. Existing remote tests were updated; no new src test files.</li><li>Covered concurrent shared-wallet reservations, Owner/Creator shared Workspace caps, NULL/0/free behavior, original price/replay/conflict, expired-held release, immutable journal sums, Video pending/failure/unknown/reconciliation, old-ledger-only refunds, Owner revision conflicts/Creator read-only access, purchased credit after expiry, and Subscription fulfillment/renewal rollback/idempotency.</li><li>Web production build and changed-source ESLint passed. Credit VI/EN: 139 keys each, no differences. Existing bundle-size/dynamic-import warnings remain.</li><li>Real Chromium with mocked APIs: direct cap edit/save; unlimited differs from 0; negative input shows inline validation on blur; stale save preserves draft and disables save; reload restores server state. Light/dark inspected; desktop 1440, tablet 768 and mobile 375 checked, mobile has no horizontal overflow. Browser artifacts are ignored/local only. No real finance API or AI called.</li><li>Local reset ran first with ROLLBACK, then committed as one transaction while all DB writers were stopped. Checksum+row count matched for all 51 preserved tables, including Admin prices and business data. Removed 332 legacy subscription rows, 215 transaction rows, 1 old grant/reservation/allocation and legacy Credit counters/limits. Four Admin price rows retained. 53 Agency subscriptions now Basic/READY; 53 wallets VERIFIED with zero available/reserved; unified grants/reservations/caps empty. No backup was created; removed test finance is not restored by the public migration. Mongo/Atlas/Task/Post untouched.</li><li>Only the new shared extension and fresh init change schema in Git. Teammates&#39; existing migration files are unchanged. The local reset script and isolated Maven/browser verification are under ignored keep-local-only, not shared setup.</li></ul><p>Not claimed: live paid AI/payment end-to-end, full application regression, runtime of every seed profile, or every expiry/period boundary. AgencyBillingWebhookPostgresTest could not initialize Testcontainers against this Docker engine (HTTP 400); the separate loopback fulfillment/renewal tests passed. IDE-written target bytecode was bypassed using an ignored isolated Maven build directory, not by changing teammates&#39; build configuration.</p><h2 id="manual-test-prerequisites" tabindex="-1">Manual test prerequisites <a class="header-anchor" href="#manual-test-prerequisites" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Manual test prerequisites&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Restart Business/Gateway/Web with the updated code. Do not run seed or init again on this local DB. The local reset is complete and intentionally refuses to run twice.</li><li>Owner opens Agency -&gt; AI Credit. Verify Workspace caps and select no cap, 0 or a positive integer. Check Manager/Creator cannot change caps and cannot read unrelated Workspaces.</li><li>Agency currently has ZERO funds. Before testing a paid action, purchase/fulfill a valid Agency subscription through the existing Subscription module; do not fabricate payment records. Existing rates retained: latest Content=3, Ambassador=10; Commercial image/Video still need enabled Admin prices before paid tests.</li><li>Free Caption/refine/adapt, Hashtag, Character sheet do not require a price or positive balance; they still require an active authorized Workspace and a verified Agency account.</li><li>After funding, use two Workspaces: caps may overlap, all actors consume Workspace used+held and the shared Agency pool. Verify successful AI charges once, authoritative failure releases once and unknown/Video pending stays held.</li><li>New teammate DB: fresh init already includes Subscription and this extension. Existing Subscription-shaped DB with no old reservations: apply the new extension after expand -&gt; catalog -&gt; provider -&gt; observability, with writers stopped. Existing DA-974 user_id schema: STOP for explicit reset/conversion review; do not blindly run expand/new extension or share the machine-local reset.</li></ol>',7)])])}const g=a(r,[["render",n]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
